A report needs the running total of the powers of three, so the loop below multiplies the power and then adds it. What does the printer output?
public class H001 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int base = 3;
        int limit = 4;
        int power = 1;
        int total = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < limit; i++) {
            power = power * base;
            total = total + power;
        }
        System.out.println(total);
    }
}

A coach wants the sum of the first five odd numbers, and the loop derives each term from the counter. What does the printer output?
public class H002 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int n = 5;
        int sum = 0;
        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
            sum = sum + (2 * i - 1);
        }
        System.out.println(sum);
    }
}

A digit loop walks a four digit value from the right, multiplying as it goes, and the two tallies are printed together. What does the printer output?
public class H003 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int value = 3045;
        int product = 1;
        int digits = 0;
        int copy = value;
        while (copy > 0) {
            product = product * (copy % 10);
            copy = copy / 10;
            digits++;
        }
        System.out.println(product + ":" + digits);
    }
}

A statistics helper adds the squares of one through four. What does the printer output?
public class H004 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int n = 4;
        int sum = 0;
        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
            sum = sum + i * i;
        }
        System.out.println(sum);
    }
}

A checksum sums the digits of a value written in base five, which is the digit sum and not the value itself. What does the printer output?
public class H005 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int value = 2025;
        int base = 5;
        int sum = 0;
        int copy = value;
        while (copy > 0) {
            sum = sum + copy % base;
            copy = copy / base;
        }
        System.out.println(sum);
    }
}

A helper must report how many factor pairs 36 has. There are five of them: 1 times 36, 2 times 18, 3 times 12, 4 times 9, and 6 times 6. The loop below prints 9 instead of 5, because it visits every divisor rather than one per pair. Which replacement for the loop header makes it print 5?
public class H006 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int n = 36;
        int pairs = 0;
        for (int d = 1; d <= n; d++) {
            if (n % d == 0) {
                pairs++;
            }
        }
        System.out.println(pairs);
    }
}

A spelling checker classifies each letter of the word QUEUE and prints the two tallies as vowels over consonants. What does the printer output?
public class H007 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String word = "QUEUE";
        int vowels = 0;
        int consonants = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < word.length(); i++) {
            char c = word.charAt(i);
            if (c == 'A' || c == 'E' || c == 'I' || c == 'O' || c == 'U') {
                vowels++;
            } else {
                consonants++;
            }
        }
        System.out.println(vowels + "/" + consonants);
    }
}

A routine rebuilds a number with its digits in the opposite order, one digit per pass. What does the printer output?
public class H008 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int value = 1207;
        int reversed = 0;
        int copy = value;
        while (copy > 0) {
            reversed = reversed * 10 + copy % 10;
            copy = copy / 10;
        }
        System.out.println(reversed);
    }
}

An exponentiation loop halves the exponent and squares a running factor, multiplying the factor into the result only on an odd exponent. What does the printer output?
public class H009 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int base = 3;
        int exponent = 5;
        int result = 1;
        int factor = base;
        int e = exponent;
        while (e > 0) {
            if (e % 2 == 1) {
                result = result * factor;
            }
            factor = factor * factor;
            e = e / 2;
        }
        System.out.println(result);
    }
}

A loop multiplies the running factorial by the counter until the product becomes divisible by thirty, and it prints the counter. What does the printer output?
public class H010 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int m = 30;
        int product = 1;
        int i = 1;
        while (product % m != 0) {
            product = product * i;
            i++;
        }
        System.out.println(i);
    }
}

A loop adds every prime below twenty, testing each candidate with a divisor scan up to its square root. What does the printer output?
public class H011 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int limit = 20;
        int total = 0;
        for (int n = 2; n < limit; n++) {
            boolean prime = true;
            for (int d = 2; d * d <= n; d++) {
                if (n % d == 0) {
                    prime = false;
                }
            }
            if (prime) {
                total = total + n;
            }
        }
        System.out.println(total);
    }
}

A sieve marks the multiples of each unmarked value as composite and counts the values that were never marked. What does the printer output?
public class H012 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int limit = 20;
        boolean[] composite = new boolean[limit];
        int count = 0;
        for (int n = 2; n < limit; n++) {
            if (!composite[n]) {
                count++;
                for (int m = n + n; m < limit; m = m + n) {
                    composite[m] = true;
                }
            }
        }
        System.out.println(count);
    }
}

A routine finds the smallest factor of a composite number by trying divisors in order and stopping at the first hit. What does the printer output?
public class H013 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int n = 91;
        int factor = n;
        for (int d = 2; d * d <= n; d++) {
            if (n % d == 0) {
                factor = d;
                break;
            }
        }
        System.out.println(factor);
    }
}

A checker adds each divisor together with its partner, and prints the sum beside the verdict. What does the printer output?
public class H014 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int n = 28;
        int sum = 1;
        for (int d = 2; d * d <= n; d++) {
            if (n % d == 0) {
                sum = sum + d + n / d;
            }
        }
        System.out.println(sum + ":" + (sum == n ? "perfect" : "other"));
    }
}

A loop reduces two values to their greatest common divisor and then scales the product to the least common multiple. What does the printer output?
public class H015 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int a = 12;
        int b = 18;
        int x = a;
        int y = b;
        while (y != 0) {
            int t = y;
            y = x % y;
            x = t;
        }
        int lcm = a / x * b;
        System.out.println(lcm);
    }
}

A helper reverses a five element row in place by swapping from both ends and stepping inward, so it should print [5, 4, 3, 2, 1]. The loop below fails before it prints anything. Which replacement for the initialisation of right makes it print [5, 4, 3, 2, 1]?
public class H016 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] values = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5};
        int left = 0;
        int right = values.length;
        while (left < right) {
            int swap = values[left];
            values[left] = values[right];
            values[right] = swap;
            left++;
            right--;
        }
        System.out.println(java.util.Arrays.toString(values));
    }
}

A loop halves an even value and triples an odd value plus one, counting rewrites until the value is one. What does the printer output?
public class H017 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int n = 6;
        int steps = 0;
        while (n != 1) {
            if (n % 2 == 0) {
                n = n / 2;
            } else {
                n = 3 * n + 1;
            }
            steps++;
        }
        System.out.println(steps);
    }
}

A checker adds the digits of 1728 and then tests whether the value divides evenly by that sum, printing the sum beside the verdict. What does the printer output?
public class H018 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int n = 1728;
        int copy = n;
        int digitSum = 0;
        while (copy > 0) {
            digitSum = digitSum + copy % 10;
            copy = copy / 10;
        }
        System.out.println(digitSum + ":" + (n % digitSum == 0 ? "harshad" : "plain"));
    }
}

