A loop repeatedly replaces a value with the sum of its digits until a single digit is left. What does the printer output?
public class H020 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int n = 9875;
        int root = n;
        while (root >= 10) {
            int sum = 0;
            int copy = root;
            while (copy > 0) {
                sum = sum + copy % 10;
                copy = copy / 10;
            }
            root = sum;
        }
        System.out.println(root);
    }
}

A loop fills an array of five cells from one using the binomial recurrence, then prints the array. What does the printer output?
public class H021 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int row = 5;
        int[] values = new int[row];
        values[0] = 1;
        for (int k = 1; k < row; k++) {
            values[k] = values[k - 1] * (row - k) / k;
        }
        System.out.println(java.util.Arrays.toString(values));
    }
}

A loop multiplies the running result by a rising numerator factor and divides by the counter to build a binomial coefficient. What does the printer output?
public class H022 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int n = 6;
        int k = 2;
        long result = 1;
        for (int i = 1; i <= k; i++) {
            result = result * (n - k + i) / i;
        }
        System.out.println(result);
    }
}

A routine adds the first n reciprocals as real numbers, so with n set to 2 the answer is 1.5 because a half is a real fraction. The loop below prints 1.0. Which replacement for the added term makes it print 1.5?
public class H023 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int n = 2;
        double total = 0.0;
        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
            total = total + 1 / i;
        }
        System.out.println(total);
    }
}

A loop adds the odd numbered terms and subtracts the even numbered ones. What does the printer output?
public class H024 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int n = 5;
        int total = 0;
        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
            if (i % 2 == 1) {
                total = total + i;
            } else {
                total = total - i;
            }
        }
        System.out.println(total);
    }
}

A loop keeps a running sum of consecutive values and a best value seen so far, restarting the run whenever the running sum turns negative. What does the printer output?
public class H025 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] values = {5, -8, 9, -4, 6};
        int best = values[0];
        int run = values[0];
        for (int i = 1; i < values.length; i++) {
            if (run < 0) {
                run = values[i];
            } else {
                run = run + values[i];
            }
            if (run > best) {
                best = run;
            }
        }
        System.out.println(best);
    }
}

A loop sums a window of three values, then slides the window one place at a time by removing the value that falls out and adding the one that falls in, keeping the best sum. What does the printer output?
public class H026 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] values = {2, 1, 5, 1, 3, 2};
        int width = 3;
        int sum = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < width; i++) {
            sum = sum + values[i];
        }
        int best = sum;
        for (int i = width; i < values.length; i++) {
            sum = sum - values[i - width] + values[i];
            if (sum > best) {
                best = sum;
            }
        }
        System.out.println(best);
    }
}

A nested scan counts the pairs of positions where the earlier value is larger than the later one. What does the printer output?
public class H027 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] values = {3, 1, 4, 1, 5};
        int inversions = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < values.length; i++) {
            for (int j = i + 1; j < values.length; j++) {
                if (values[i] > values[j]) {
                    inversions++;
                }
            }
        }
        System.out.println(inversions);
    }
}

A loop starts one pointer at each end of a six element row, adds the two values it points at, and steps both pointers inward until they meet. What does the printer output?
public class H028 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] values = {1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11};
        int left = 0;
        int right = values.length - 1;
        int total = 0;
        while (left < right) {
            total = total + values[left] + values[right];
            left++;
            right--;
        }
        System.out.println(total);
    }
}

A partition loop steps the left pointer over values that are already in place and swaps a misplaced positive with a misplaced negative, then prints the row. What does the printer output?
public class H029 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] values = {-1, 2, -3, 4, -5, 6};
        int left = 0;
        int right = values.length - 1;
        while (left < right) {
            if (values[left] < 0) {
                left++;
            } else if (values[right] < 0) {
                int swap = values[left];
                values[left] = values[right];
                values[right] = swap;
                left++;
                right--;
            } else {
                right--;
            }
        }
        System.out.println(java.util.Arrays.toString(values));
    }
}

A single pass keeps the largest and second largest values and prints them as largest over second. What does the printer output?
public class H030 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] values = {12, 7, 19, 7, 25};
        int largest = values[0];
        int second = values[0];
        for (int i = 1; i < values.length; i++) {
            if (values[i] > largest) {
                second = largest;
                largest = values[i];
            } else if (values[i] > second) {
                second = values[i];
            }
        }
        System.out.println(largest + ":" + second);
    }
}

A tally counts how many words have each length, and the loop runs one index past the text so that the final word is flushed as well. What does the printer output?
public class H031 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] counts = new int[5];
        String text = "a bb ccc dddd";
        int length = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i <= text.length(); i++) {
            if (i == text.length() || text.charAt(i) == ' ') {
                counts[length]++;
                length = 0;
            } else {
                length++;
            }
        }
        System.out.println(java.util.Arrays.toString(counts));
    }
}

A loop measures each word as it goes and keeps the length and the starting position of the longest one, then prints the two. What does the printer output?
public class H032 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String text = "the quick brown fox";
        int longest = 0;
        int start = 0;
        int best = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i <= text.length(); i++) {
            if (i == text.length() || text.charAt(i) == ' ') {
                if (i - start > longest) {
                    longest = i - start;
                    best = start;
                }
                start = i + 1;
            }
        }
        System.out.println(longest + ":" + text.substring(best, best + longest));
    }
}

A helper takes the last word of a sentence by scanning backwards to the space before it, and repeats until nothing is left. What does the printer output?
public class H033 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String text = "one two three";
        String result = "";
        int end = text.length();
        while (end > 0) {
            int start = end - 1;
            while (start > 0 && text.charAt(start - 1) != ' ') {
                start--;
            }
            if (result.isEmpty()) {
                result = text.substring(start, end);
            } else {
                result = result + " " + text.substring(start, end);
            }
            end = start - 1;
        }
        System.out.println(result);
    }
}

