A parser walks a mixed code and sends each character to one of two strings according to a character test. Which line correctly describes what the printer outputs?
public class H035 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String code = "a1b22c333";
        String digits = "";
        String letters = "";
        for (int i = 0; i < code.length(); i++) {
            char c = code.charAt(i);
            if (Character.isDigit(c)) {
                digits = digits + c;
            } else {
                letters = letters + c;
            }
        }
        System.out.println(digits + "|" + letters);
    }
}

A loop takes each position in turn, counts how often that character appears anywhere in the text, and stops at the first character whose count is one. What does the printer output?
public class H036 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String text = "aabcb";
        int first = -1;
        for (int i = 0; i < text.length(); i++) {
            int count = 0;
            for (int j = 0; j < text.length(); j++) {
                if (text.charAt(j) == text.charAt(i)) {
                    count++;
                }
            }
            if (count == 1) {
                first = i;
                break;
            }
        }
        System.out.println(text.charAt(first));
    }
}

A loop keeps the length of the current run of equal values and the longest run seen so far, then prints the longest. What does the printer output?
public class H037 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] values = {1, 1, 2, 2, 2, 3, 3};
        int best = 0;
        int run = 0;
        int previous = -99;
        for (int i = 0; i < values.length; i++) {
            if (values[i] == previous) {
                run++;
            } else {
                run = 1;
            }
            if (run > best) {
                best = run;
            }
            previous = values[i];
        }
        System.out.println(best);
    }
}

