A helper converts a number below one hundred into Roman numerals, where 88 is LXXXVIII because the L and the three X symbols each repeat. The loop below prints LXIXVIVI because it uses every symbol at most once. Which replacement for the inner test makes it print LXXXVIII?
public class H041 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] values = {50, 40, 10, 9, 5, 4, 1};
        String[] symbols = {"L", "XL", "X", "IX", "V", "IV", "I"};
        int n = 88;
        String roman = "";
        for (int k = 0; k < values.length; k++) {
            if (n >= values[k]) {
                roman = roman + symbols[k];
                n = n - values[k];
            }
        }
        System.out.println(roman);
    }
}

A loop adds every divisor of 36 to a running total, counting a square root divisor only once, and stops when the trial divisor passes the square root. What does the printer output?
public class H042 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int n = 36;
        int total = 0;
        for (int d = 1; d * d <= n; d++) {
            if (n % d == 0) {
                total = total + d;
                if (d != n / d) {
                    total = total + n / d;
                }
            }
        }
        System.out.println(total);
    }
}

